WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.680
Application security matters in payment environments because web applications often sit

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.260
directly in front of checkout flows, payment records, identity data, administrative tools,

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.600
and integrations that support the cardholder data environment.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.380
A single application weakness can expose cardholder data, enable fraud,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.920
or create evidence gaps during assessment.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.580
OWASP provides community-driven application security guidance.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.960
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a shared vocabulary for high-impact web application risks and

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.540
helps developers,

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.280
security engineers, DevOps teams, and compliance teams prioritize review and remediation.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.500
PCI DSS v4.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:46.160
0 is a payment security standard focused on protecting account data and reducing risk

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.460
across the cardholder data environment.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:53.800
It includes requirements for secure configuration, data protection, access control,

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.940
authentication, logging, monitoring, vulnerability management,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.160
and secure software development.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.180
The cardholder data environment includes people, processes, and technologies that store,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.720
process, transmit, or can impact the security of cardholder data.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:15.060
Application teams need to understand when their code, infrastructure, APIs,

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.000
or operational tooling can affect that environment.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.340
This course pairs each OWASP Top 10 category with payment-oriented attack examples,

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:29.400
practical mitigations, and selected PCI DSS v4. 0 requirement mappings.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.420
The mappings are awareness aids, not a substitute for a formal PCI DSS assessment.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.480
Use OWASP categories to organize application risk discussions.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.660
Use PCI DSS requirements to connect security engineering work to payment protection

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.080
obligations.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:50.260
Validate all mappings against the organization's real cardholder data environment and

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.120
assessment scope. Selected PCI DSS mappings for this topic include Req.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:03.980
6.2 - Secure software development processes; Req. 12.2 - Targeted risk analyses; Req.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.320
12.5 - PCI DSS scope and responsibilities.
